1
00:00:04,471 --> 00:00:07,107
Doctors, please listen carefully.

2
00:00:07,173 --> 00:00:09,843
The days where doctors
were called <i>"oisha-sama"</i>

3
00:00:09,909 --> 00:00:12,746
and where they only had
to treat illness are over.

4
00:00:12,812 --> 00:00:15,482
The focus of future medical care
is strictly with <i>"kanja-sama."</i>

5
00:00:15,548 --> 00:00:16,850
KANEKO TERAYAMA
MANAGER

6
00:00:16,950 --> 00:00:20,620
The most important thing
to a hospital is patient satisfaction.

7
00:00:20,787 --> 00:00:23,757
In other words, quality of life.

8
00:00:23,823 --> 00:00:25,091
HIDEKI KAJI - SURGERY #2 - TEACHER
MAMORU HARA - SURGERY #2 - ASSISTANT

9
00:00:25,158 --> 00:00:27,260
The basics of medical care
are sincerity and service.

10
00:00:27,327 --> 00:00:28,228
HIROMI JONOUCHI
ANESTHESIOLOGIST

11
00:00:28,294 --> 00:00:31,664
Listen closely by paying attention
to the patient's wishes.

12
00:00:31,731 --> 00:00:36,302
Then, by reaching out
to the patient's feelings, sympathize.

13
00:00:36,803 --> 00:00:40,507
These two items are the most important.

14
00:00:40,974 --> 00:00:45,111
Make sure to avoid one-sided explanations
and talking down to patients.

15
00:00:45,211 --> 00:00:46,212
MICHIKO DAIMON
FREELANCE SURGEON

16
00:00:46,279 --> 00:00:49,616
Common sense and rules
can't be applied to monster patients...

17
00:00:49,682 --> 00:00:51,317
MONSTER PATIENT - PATIENT WHO MAKES
OR DOES UNREASONABLE REQUESTS OR ACTIONS

18
00:00:51,384 --> 00:00:53,353
...who are furious and dissatisfied.

19
00:00:53,420 --> 00:00:56,056
First, listen attentively and sympathize,

20
00:00:56,256 --> 00:00:58,425
then calm them down.

21
00:00:58,491 --> 00:00:59,626
At that time,

22
00:01:00,026 --> 00:01:05,131
words like "so,"
"but," "then" and "that's why,"

23
00:01:05,565 --> 00:01:07,267
they are likely to be used,

24
00:01:07,567 --> 00:01:10,470
but all of these words are taboo.

25
00:01:10,537 --> 00:01:11,938
I'll repeat again.

26
00:01:12,072 --> 00:01:14,441
"So," "but,"

27
00:01:14,507 --> 00:01:15,742
"then", "that's why."

28
00:01:15,809 --> 00:01:16,843
RYUNOSUKE BUSUJIMA
HOSPITAL CHIEF

29
00:01:17,310 --> 00:01:19,612
All of these words are taboo.

30
00:01:20,713 --> 00:01:22,415
Dr. Kaji?

31
00:01:23,316 --> 00:01:25,151
What is the most important thing
for a hospital?

32
00:01:26,653 --> 00:01:28,922
Uh... patient satisfaction.

33
00:01:28,988 --> 00:01:31,091
<i>Kanja... sa-ma!</i>

34
00:01:31,157 --> 00:01:32,125
My apologies.

35
00:01:32,692 --> 00:01:37,130
<i>Kanja... sama, </i>satisfaction
and their quality of life.

36
00:01:37,430 --> 00:01:39,365
Next, Dr. Jonouchi.

37
00:01:39,632 --> 00:01:40,800
What are the basics of medical care?

38
00:01:41,768 --> 00:01:43,570
- Sincerity and service.
- Yes.

39
00:01:44,003 --> 00:01:46,306
- Dr. Hara?
- Listening attentively and sympathy.

40
00:01:46,406 --> 00:01:47,907
Yes, that's right.

41
00:01:48,308 --> 00:01:50,844
What do we do to prevent monster patients?

42
00:01:51,311 --> 00:01:53,980
<i>- </i>Listen attentively and sympathize.
- That's right.

43
00:01:54,047 --> 00:01:56,382
Now then, let's all repeat together.

44
00:01:56,649 --> 00:01:58,118
Ready, set... go!

45
00:01:58,885 --> 00:02:00,887
<i>Kanja-sama </i>satisfaction!

46
00:02:01,688 --> 00:02:02,822
Quality of life!

47
00:02:03,990 --> 00:02:05,758
Sincerity and service!

48
00:02:06,926 --> 00:02:08,628
Listen attentively and sympathize!

49
00:02:08,695 --> 00:02:11,097
That's good, thank you.

50
00:02:11,831 --> 00:02:14,000
Daimon. Daimon!

51
00:02:14,667 --> 00:02:16,236
You were sleeping just now, right?

52
00:02:16,302 --> 00:02:17,470
It seems...

53
00:02:19,239 --> 00:02:22,675
a medical license is completely
unnecessary for this conference.

54
00:02:22,775 --> 00:02:24,310
I'll pass.

55
00:02:26,212 --> 00:02:28,081
Wait. Wait right there!

56
00:02:28,815 --> 00:02:32,051
Who the hell do you think we're holding
this emergency compliance meeting for?

57
00:02:32,118 --> 00:02:32,952
Huh?

58
00:02:33,019 --> 00:02:34,587
Seems you feel no remorse.

59
00:02:34,654 --> 00:02:35,822
TAKASHI TORII
#2 SURGERY CHIEF - PROFESSOR

60
00:02:35,889 --> 00:02:37,957
Manager, please show her that video.

61
00:02:38,024 --> 00:02:38,858
Yes.

62
00:02:42,295 --> 00:02:46,065
This is a video
of an informed-consent meeting

63
00:02:46,132 --> 00:02:47,233
held one week ago.

64
00:02:47,333 --> 00:02:50,470
You're kidding... a hidden camera?

65
00:02:50,770 --> 00:02:54,140
All meetings are recorded
with the patient's approval.

66
00:02:54,674 --> 00:02:56,309
It's a precaution against lawsuits.

67
00:02:57,677 --> 00:02:59,646
<i>But if we do this quick and easy,</i>

68
00:02:59,712 --> 00:03:02,048
<i>Mr. Yano's prostate cancer</i>
<i>will be radically cured.</i>

69
00:03:02,282 --> 00:03:04,384
<i>Did you say quick and easy?</i>

70
00:03:05,051 --> 00:03:08,988
<i>Doctor, you have no understanding</i>
<i>of how a cancer patient feels!</i>

71
00:03:09,055 --> 00:03:11,624
<i>That's why, mother, keep out of this.</i>

72
00:03:11,891 --> 00:03:14,160
<i>Your son is a grown man.</i>

73
00:03:15,028 --> 00:03:17,263
<i>To be honest, surgery is scary.</i>

74
00:03:18,164 --> 00:03:19,299
<i>But...</i>

75
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:23,203
<i>if you have the surgery now,</i>
<i>you'll be completely healthy.</i>

76
00:03:25,405 --> 00:03:28,575
<i>But if you don't get the surgery,</i>
<i>the cancer will surely progress.</i>

77
00:03:29,742 --> 00:03:31,010
<i>I don't want to die!</i>

78
00:03:31,077 --> 00:03:33,379
<i>Then sign this consent form.</i>

79
00:03:33,513 --> 00:03:34,647
<i>Dr. Daimon.</i>

80
00:03:36,683 --> 00:03:37,684
<i>Mama!</i>

81
00:03:37,750 --> 00:03:40,954
<i>So are you doing it, or are you not?</i>

82
00:03:41,487 --> 00:03:42,488
<i>Which one?</i>

83
00:03:42,956 --> 00:03:45,124
SO - BUT - THEN - THAT'S WHY

84
00:03:48,061 --> 00:03:49,062
Scary!

85
00:03:49,996 --> 00:03:51,764
No matter what situation.

86
00:03:51,831 --> 00:03:56,135
Unheard of! "So," "but," "then,"
"that's why." A string of taboo words.

87
00:03:56,202 --> 00:03:57,737
But this patient

88
00:03:57,971 --> 00:04:01,207
went home after a successful
prostate cancer surgery.

89
00:04:02,075 --> 00:04:02,942
Right?

90
00:04:03,409 --> 00:04:04,444
HIKARU MORIMOTO
#2 SURGERY - ASSISTANT

91
00:04:04,510 --> 00:04:08,514
We received a letter of complaint
from the patient's mother.

92
00:04:09,315 --> 00:04:13,753
"My son was threatened by a Dr. Daimon
to sign the consent form,

93
00:04:13,820 --> 00:04:17,023
and he suffered deep psychological scars."

94
00:04:17,090 --> 00:04:20,093
Why? Even though I saved his life.

95
00:04:20,159 --> 00:04:21,694
That's called arrogance.

96
00:04:21,794 --> 00:04:24,364
I'm saying even if the surgery succeeds,
the patient might sue us

97
00:04:24,430 --> 00:04:25,732
if they aren't satisfied!

98
00:04:26,199 --> 00:04:27,300
<i>Kanja-sama.</i>

99
00:04:28,134 --> 00:04:30,403
Ah, exactly as you say.

100
00:04:30,470 --> 00:04:32,305
Well, that's enough for now.

101
00:04:33,640 --> 00:04:37,043
But... we are worried about lawsuits.

102
00:04:38,311 --> 00:04:41,914
It's a serious matter
that affects business, so...

103
00:04:42,181 --> 00:04:43,016
Certainly.

104
00:04:43,082 --> 00:04:44,550
- Certainly.
- Certainly.

105
00:04:47,587 --> 00:04:48,421
Daimon.

106
00:04:49,255 --> 00:04:50,957
I'm counting on you, too.

107
00:04:57,497 --> 00:04:58,498
Certainly.

108
00:05:05,204 --> 00:05:07,040
Just kidding...

109
00:05:16,349 --> 00:05:19,385
Since when did doctors become
part of the service industry?

110
00:05:19,452 --> 00:05:21,587
Even if you do
what you think is best for patients,

111
00:05:21,688 --> 00:05:23,856
if they're not happy,
they can still sue you?

112
00:05:23,923 --> 00:05:25,591
Isn't that sad?

113
00:05:27,860 --> 00:05:31,297
But it's useless telling that to you,
Dr. Daimon.

114
00:05:31,764 --> 00:05:32,632
Yep, useless.

115
00:05:33,099 --> 00:05:33,933
Yes.

116
00:05:38,438 --> 00:05:41,741
I'm Hanayama, I was admitted
to the special room today.

117
00:05:41,808 --> 00:05:46,312
I've cooked some food for you today
just to introduce myself.

118
00:05:46,379 --> 00:05:47,714
It's Mitsue Hanayama.

119
00:05:48,181 --> 00:05:50,116
- Who?
- You don't know her?

120
00:05:50,516 --> 00:05:52,018
She's a pretty cooking expert...

121
00:05:52,085 --> 00:05:53,086
MITSUE HANAYAMA
COOKING EXPERT

122
00:05:53,152 --> 00:05:55,054
...who appears on TV
and has lots of people reading her blog!

123
00:05:55,521 --> 00:05:58,358
I put extra special effort into this!
Please help yourself.

124
00:05:58,424 --> 00:06:02,128
Wow! It's an honor to be able
to enjoy Ms. Hanayama's cooking.

125
00:06:02,228 --> 00:06:05,331
- Help yourself.
- Wow!

126
00:06:05,398 --> 00:06:07,900
- Well, let's eat.
- Let's eat.

127
00:06:13,506 --> 00:06:14,507
How is it?

128
00:06:16,075 --> 00:06:18,444
It's delicious as I thought it would be!

129
00:06:20,079 --> 00:06:24,550
- This croquette, too!
- It's a foie gras and natto colosseum.

130
00:06:26,819 --> 00:06:28,554
Whatever, it's exquisite!

131
00:06:31,624 --> 00:06:33,226
For the lady doctor there too,

132
00:06:33,326 --> 00:06:35,895
forget about that onigiri
and have some of this.

133
00:06:44,270 --> 00:06:47,306
- Yeah, this is better.
- Don't be shy now.

134
00:06:47,373 --> 00:06:50,576
Food that doesn't make you happy
impoverishes the soul.

135
00:06:50,676 --> 00:06:51,644
I'm really fine.

136
00:06:51,711 --> 00:06:54,013
Why? Foie gras and natto colosseum

137
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:57,016
is one of my most popular recipes.

138
00:06:58,151 --> 00:06:59,719
The naming is strange...

139
00:07:00,853 --> 00:07:01,788
and it tastes bad.

140
00:07:06,426 --> 00:07:07,493
Daimon!

141
00:07:07,693 --> 00:07:09,562
It has nice naming, right?

142
00:07:10,329 --> 00:07:11,831
- Right?
- Yes!

143
00:07:14,066 --> 00:07:16,836
It doesn't seem to suit
the lady doctor's tastes.

144
00:07:16,903 --> 00:07:20,406
Everyone, please help yourself!

145
00:07:21,207 --> 00:07:26,846
This lady doctor doesn't like the taste
of Ms. Hanayama's happy cooking.

146
00:07:27,046 --> 00:07:31,951
As you can see, she's the type of person
who likes eating while looking at organs.

147
00:07:36,289 --> 00:07:39,325
Okay, I'm off
to intestinal blockage surgery.

148
00:07:39,492 --> 00:07:41,060
Hey, w-wait!

149
00:07:50,736 --> 00:07:54,073
<i>This is the story</i>
<i>of a lone wolf woman doctor.</i>

150
00:07:55,241 --> 00:07:57,610
Is the food ready yet?
How long am I gonna wait?

151
00:07:57,677 --> 00:07:59,011
I'm sorry, but please wait.

152
00:07:59,078 --> 00:08:00,179
SONOKA CHIBA
CHIEF NURSE

153
00:08:00,246 --> 00:08:02,081
I'm hungry, and what will you do
if I become sicker?

154
00:08:02,148 --> 00:08:03,349
Ow, ow...

155
00:08:03,549 --> 00:08:04,584
It's cold here, please--

156
00:08:04,650 --> 00:08:06,486
Shut up! Hurry and bring me my food!

157
00:08:06,552 --> 00:08:08,521
I never asked for your help!

158
00:08:10,723 --> 00:08:13,226
<i>Medicine in university hospitals</i>
<i>has weakened,</i>

159
00:08:13,893 --> 00:08:16,128
<i>and even medicine, which deals with life,</i>

160
00:08:16,195 --> 00:08:18,798
<i>has already entered the era</i>
<i>of the law of the jungle.</i>

161
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:24,737
<i>To fill this critical shortage</i>
<i>in the medical field, freelance,</i>

162
00:08:25,605 --> 00:08:28,875
<i>in other words,</i>
<i>lone wolf doctors, have emerged.</i>

163
00:08:31,277 --> 00:08:33,112
<i>For example, this woman.</i>

164
00:08:34,881 --> 00:08:37,683
<i>She hates groups, she hates authority,</i>

165
00:08:38,384 --> 00:08:39,886
<i>and she hates restraints.</i>

166
00:08:40,653 --> 00:08:45,024
<i>Her weapons are her specialty license</i>
<i>and her skill to work her way up.</i>

167
00:08:46,092 --> 00:08:48,528
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

168
00:08:49,962 --> 00:08:50,796
<i>Also known as...</i>

169
00:08:52,598 --> 00:08:54,133
<i>Doctor X.</i>

170
00:09:02,775 --> 00:09:05,711
DOCTOR X SURGEON MICHIKO DAIMON
EPISODE 3

171
00:09:08,681 --> 00:09:10,683
As a measure to reinforce compliance,

172
00:09:10,750 --> 00:09:13,886
we've placed five suggestion boxes
throughout the hospital.

173
00:09:13,953 --> 00:09:18,257
The following are...
today's complaints and opinions.

174
00:09:18,324 --> 00:09:20,593
The outpatient wait time is too long.

175
00:09:20,860 --> 00:09:23,729
I can't sleep because
the neighboring patient snores too loudly.

176
00:09:23,930 --> 00:09:26,699
All nurses and staff are ugly.
Fix this somehow.

177
00:09:27,099 --> 00:09:28,701
How rude.

178
00:09:29,468 --> 00:09:33,472
Anyways, please take appropriate steps
so they don't become monster patients.

179
00:09:33,539 --> 00:09:34,874
- Certainly.
- Certainly.

180
00:09:35,241 --> 00:09:40,580
These days, Internet forums and blogs
have a big impact as well.

181
00:09:42,048 --> 00:09:44,917
We will keep watch 24 hours a day.

182
00:09:46,886 --> 00:09:51,424
<i>Even at Teito University Third Hospital,</i>
<i>where I've been admitted for testing,</i>

183
00:09:51,724 --> 00:09:54,026
<i>my cooking has been getting great reviews.</i>

184
00:09:54,961 --> 00:09:57,563
<i>In particular, the single doctors</i>

185
00:09:57,897 --> 00:09:59,932
<i>were quite impressed.</i>

186
00:10:01,534 --> 00:10:04,236
<i>They said, "Delicious, exquisite."</i>

187
00:10:05,204 --> 00:10:08,641
"But there was
this one obnoxious lady doctor."

188
00:10:08,708 --> 00:10:10,176
AKIRA KAMBARA
DOCTOR REFERRAL AGENCY CHIEF

189
00:10:10,242 --> 00:10:11,978
Isn't that about you, Michiko?

190
00:10:12,044 --> 00:10:14,046
- What?
- "This lady doctor

191
00:10:14,413 --> 00:10:17,717
criticized my cooking
and kept gorging on her onigiri.

192
00:10:17,783 --> 00:10:22,822
She's probably a surgery freak who doesn't
have a boyfriend she can cook for

193
00:10:23,289 --> 00:10:28,094
and she's probably leading a lonely life."
She said that.

194
00:10:28,494 --> 00:10:31,964
Mitsue Hanayama is probably a single woman
in her 30s too, right?

195
00:10:34,667 --> 00:10:37,470
Akira, why are you reading this blog?

196
00:10:37,870 --> 00:10:43,242
I tried making this "Exquisite Squash
that Grabs Mens' Stomachs."

197
00:10:43,709 --> 00:10:46,012
It's definitely gonna be bad.

198
00:10:47,513 --> 00:10:49,615
No, it's very good.

199
00:10:50,116 --> 00:10:50,950
Good?

200
00:11:01,527 --> 00:11:02,728
It's delicious. Why?

201
00:11:03,562 --> 00:11:04,964
Let's make this next.

202
00:11:05,698 --> 00:11:11,671
"Handsome Mens' Sauté
to Fulfill Womens' Stomachs."

203
00:11:13,806 --> 00:11:16,909
This is really delicious. Why?

204
00:11:17,309 --> 00:11:20,813
INCREASE GIRL POWER
COOKING EXPERT MITSUE HANAYAMA'S RECIPES

205
00:11:21,280 --> 00:11:24,650
Stage 2 esophageal cancer, huh?
Has the patient been told?

206
00:11:25,051 --> 00:11:28,287
Yes. Ms. Hanayama took it in stride,

207
00:11:28,854 --> 00:11:31,557
esophageal cancer is hard to take
for a cooking expert.

208
00:11:31,624 --> 00:11:33,993
She should have the surgery
as soon as possible.

209
00:11:34,126 --> 00:11:34,960
Yes.

210
00:11:35,127 --> 00:11:36,429
It's strange...

211
00:11:37,029 --> 00:11:39,765
Esophageal cancer shouldn't cause
a taste disorder.

212
00:11:39,832 --> 00:11:41,067
What are you saying?

213
00:11:42,068 --> 00:11:44,937
I heard you got into trouble with
this patient as soon as she was admitted.

214
00:11:45,071 --> 00:11:47,339
I just said that her food tasted bad.

215
00:11:47,406 --> 00:11:50,342
That's your problem.
You hurt the patient's pride.

216
00:11:50,409 --> 00:11:52,812
She'll get sued eventually.

217
00:11:54,280 --> 00:11:56,415
You ate her food, didn't you?

218
00:11:58,117 --> 00:11:59,952
Did you think it was delicious?

219
00:12:00,720 --> 00:12:02,154
Everyone's taste buds are strange.

220
00:12:02,221 --> 00:12:03,489
Probably...

221
00:12:04,890 --> 00:12:05,725
Idiot!

222
00:12:06,625 --> 00:12:10,963
We were just giving
the patient lip service to keep her happy.

223
00:12:11,564 --> 00:12:14,233
- It did taste different, right?
- Yeah.

224
00:12:14,734 --> 00:12:17,536
I could only taste spices in my croquette.

225
00:12:17,603 --> 00:12:19,605
Maybe those spices are trendy now?

226
00:12:19,672 --> 00:12:21,707
What? You guys thought the same.

227
00:12:21,807 --> 00:12:23,709
We can't say that
to a cooking pro, though.

228
00:12:23,776 --> 00:12:26,479
With regards to compliance,
you were correct.

229
00:12:27,313 --> 00:12:29,682
Her recipes are good,

230
00:12:30,182 --> 00:12:32,485
but the food she herself cooks is bad.

231
00:12:32,551 --> 00:12:33,686
Professor...

232
00:12:34,453 --> 00:12:36,455
she's planning to do the surgery.

233
00:12:36,856 --> 00:12:37,723
Don't joke.

234
00:12:38,190 --> 00:12:41,927
Good psychological care is needed
for female patients like that.

235
00:12:42,561 --> 00:12:44,563
Hara, you do the operation.

236
00:12:44,630 --> 00:12:45,531
Yes!

237
00:12:45,598 --> 00:12:47,633
The assistant is, let's see...

238
00:12:49,869 --> 00:12:51,137
Daimon.

239
00:12:51,704 --> 00:12:53,405
You'll be Hara's assistant.

240
00:12:53,472 --> 00:12:55,407
- What? Me?
- What?

241
00:12:56,308 --> 00:12:59,979
Is it really okay
to have her as the assistant?

242
00:13:00,379 --> 00:13:01,814
I'm off to an operation.

243
00:13:03,382 --> 00:13:07,620
Hara, take this chance to teach her
what medical care really is.

244
00:13:07,987 --> 00:13:12,591
Understood. I'll teach her medical care
that reaches out to patients!

245
00:13:12,658 --> 00:13:15,728
However, don't say anything
in front of the patient.

246
00:13:15,795 --> 00:13:18,631
- Just keep quiet and do your work.
- This...

247
00:13:24,537 --> 00:13:26,739
Let's keep my illness a close secret.

248
00:13:27,339 --> 00:13:31,811
I, Mitsue Hanayama, have to preserve
an image to pursue happiness and health.

249
00:13:32,645 --> 00:13:33,479
Yes.

250
00:13:35,314 --> 00:13:37,316
- Come in.
- Excuse me.

251
00:13:38,417 --> 00:13:41,086
- Ms. Hanayama, your food.
- Thanks.

252
00:13:53,666 --> 00:13:54,834
What is this?

253
00:13:55,668 --> 00:13:57,203
Does this have any flavor at all?

254
00:13:59,839 --> 00:14:02,174
- I won't eat this.
- But...

255
00:14:05,244 --> 00:14:08,681
Mr. Nakamura, does the scar
from your surgery still hurt?

256
00:14:08,747 --> 00:14:10,516
Don't bear it if it hurts, just tell us.

257
00:14:10,583 --> 00:14:12,284
- Thank you very much!
- It's nothing.

258
00:14:13,252 --> 00:14:16,522
Oh! Ms. Saito, you look good today.

259
00:14:16,589 --> 00:14:19,792
Doctor, my grandchild came today.

260
00:14:19,859 --> 00:14:24,330
- I got a shoulder massage!
- Is that so? That must've been nice.

261
00:14:24,763 --> 00:14:27,032
- Thank you very much.
- Thanks.

262
00:14:32,104 --> 00:14:35,274
Talking with patients
is part of medical care, too.

263
00:14:36,008 --> 00:14:38,611
If you can connect with each other,
treatment is easier.

264
00:14:44,016 --> 00:14:48,687
Well, I suppose you don't want to do
things that don't need a medical license.

265
00:14:48,754 --> 00:14:50,756
Yes, it's a waste of my time.

266
00:14:51,223 --> 00:14:55,961
You'll learn soon that a basic point of
medical care is reaching out to patients.

267
00:14:57,796 --> 00:14:58,631
Hey.

268
00:14:59,899 --> 00:15:01,333
Yes.

269
00:15:06,238 --> 00:15:08,340
Thank you for waiting.
I am Hara, your primary surgeon.

270
00:15:09,141 --> 00:15:11,644
- Oh.
- This is my assistant, Daimon.

271
00:15:11,777 --> 00:15:14,780
Doctor, just in case anything happens,

272
00:15:15,047 --> 00:15:17,816
I'm having my lawyer attend this meeting.

273
00:15:18,450 --> 00:15:19,351
Here's my card.

274
00:15:22,187 --> 00:15:24,189
Thank you. So you're a lawyer.

275
00:15:24,390 --> 00:15:27,393
Yes, as there's a lot of medical trouble
these days.

276
00:15:31,330 --> 00:15:35,200
Well then, let me start
the explanation of this surgery.

277
00:15:36,669 --> 00:15:40,139
Ms. Hanayama's cancer is in
this part of the esophagus.

278
00:15:41,040 --> 00:15:43,042
After removing the cancer,

279
00:15:44,209 --> 00:15:45,978
by stretching the stomach,

280
00:15:46,445 --> 00:15:49,148
we will perform a surgery
to reconstruct the esophagus.

281
00:15:49,214 --> 00:15:51,350
Is this surgery safe?

282
00:15:51,483 --> 00:15:55,287
Professionally, she's concerned
about any problems with eating.

283
00:15:55,354 --> 00:15:56,855
Well, that's...

284
00:15:58,524 --> 00:16:02,895
Since the stomach size is reduced,
you may experience loss of appetite

285
00:16:02,962 --> 00:16:05,130
and weight loss after the surgery.

286
00:16:05,564 --> 00:16:09,068
In rare cases, voice abnormalities
or dysphagia may occur...

287
00:16:09,134 --> 00:16:10,536
RECURRENT NERVE PARALYSIS - PARALYSIS
OF NERVES THAT MOVE THE VOCAL CHORDS

288
00:16:10,602 --> 00:16:12,304
...due to recurrent nerve paralysis.

289
00:16:12,371 --> 00:16:13,339
DYSPHAGIA

290
00:16:13,405 --> 00:16:14,239
What's that?

291
00:16:14,306 --> 00:16:16,108
Difficulty in chewing and swallowing.

292
00:16:17,076 --> 00:16:21,914
If I get those disorders,
what happens to me as a cooking expert?

293
00:16:22,815 --> 00:16:24,283
I understand your worries.

294
00:16:24,350 --> 00:16:27,820
But that doesn't mean
all patients have this after surgery.

295
00:16:28,387 --> 00:16:31,557
We will do the surgery
with meticulous care,

296
00:16:31,957 --> 00:16:33,625
let's do our best together.

297
00:16:33,692 --> 00:16:35,561
How can you say that?

298
00:16:36,095 --> 00:16:38,230
Why don't you try having this cancer, too?

299
00:16:38,297 --> 00:16:40,466
If you don't, you don't know how I feel!

300
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:43,602
I apologize for my insensitivity.

301
00:16:44,203 --> 00:16:47,206
I won't do it after all.
I won't have the surgery.

302
00:16:48,140 --> 00:16:48,974
What?

303
00:16:51,043 --> 00:16:53,612
There's treatment
other than surgery, right?

304
00:16:54,380 --> 00:16:57,049
We'll switch to anti-cancer drugs
and radiation treatment.

305
00:16:57,683 --> 00:17:00,786
But still, if you switch
to internal medicine treatment...

306
00:17:02,121 --> 00:17:03,756
If you don't have the surgery,

307
00:17:03,822 --> 00:17:05,858
the possibility
of a radical cure diminishes.

308
00:17:06,325 --> 00:17:09,328
We can not sign the consent form.

309
00:17:17,936 --> 00:17:18,837
Understood.

310
00:17:19,338 --> 00:17:20,806
No way. Why?

311
00:17:20,906 --> 00:17:22,174
You stay out of this.

312
00:17:23,709 --> 00:17:26,345
Let me operate on you. I'll do well.

313
00:17:27,279 --> 00:17:31,250
You're the one who said
my food tasted bad, right?

314
00:17:31,884 --> 00:17:32,851
I can't trust you.

315
00:17:35,854 --> 00:17:36,822
Ms. Hanayama...

316
00:17:37,956 --> 00:17:39,358
you have trouble tasting, yes?

317
00:17:40,959 --> 00:17:42,728
Have you noticed symptoms?

318
00:17:43,362 --> 00:17:45,431
I'm a cooking expert! How rude!

319
00:17:45,497 --> 00:17:47,566
Daimon! I apologize.

320
00:17:47,833 --> 00:17:51,537
- I'm suing! Sue her for defamation!
- Very well.

321
00:17:52,204 --> 00:17:54,039
You should have it removed!

322
00:17:54,606 --> 00:17:57,409
Anyways, I'm definitely
not having the surgery.

323
00:18:07,486 --> 00:18:08,420
You idiot!

324
00:18:08,487 --> 00:18:11,290
We got a demand for an apology
from the lawyer via certified mail!

325
00:18:12,791 --> 00:18:14,526
Does an apology mean money?

326
00:18:15,194 --> 00:18:17,262
That attitude. No,

327
00:18:17,596 --> 00:18:21,300
your mere presence here
is non-compliance.

328
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:23,602
I just told her the truth.

329
00:18:24,269 --> 00:18:25,604
That's why you're an idiot!

330
00:18:25,671 --> 00:18:30,008
What kind of idiot doctor goes on
babbling the truth in front of patients?

331
00:18:30,742 --> 00:18:34,179
- I'm very sorry. In my presence, too.
- A surgeon is worth their skill, no?

332
00:18:34,379 --> 00:18:37,416
Besides, if she has the surgery,
she'll be 100 percent cured.

333
00:18:37,483 --> 00:18:39,384
In this case, it doesn't matter!

334
00:18:39,685 --> 00:18:43,755
Whether the patient is cured or not,
as long as we aren't sued, who cares?

335
00:18:43,822 --> 00:18:45,090
- Manager.
- Yes!

336
00:18:46,291 --> 00:18:50,295
I'm terribly sorry.
Of all people, I lost my composure.

337
00:18:51,763 --> 00:18:54,700
Please be more careful in the future.

338
00:18:58,570 --> 00:19:02,641
I have a gathering to attend
at the main campus after this,

339
00:19:02,708 --> 00:19:03,909
so please excuse me.

340
00:19:03,976 --> 00:19:05,777
- Bring the car around!
- Yes!

341
00:19:17,456 --> 00:19:21,326
You know, you always cause trouble,
but you have insurance, right?

342
00:19:22,561 --> 00:19:23,795
Insurance? What's that?

343
00:19:24,263 --> 00:19:26,365
Medical malpractice insurance.

344
00:19:26,698 --> 00:19:28,567
In case you get sued.

345
00:19:29,001 --> 00:19:31,103
What? Don't tell me you don't?

346
00:19:31,770 --> 00:19:33,238
- No.
- What?

347
00:19:33,906 --> 00:19:36,441
- What did you say?
- You idiot!

348
00:19:36,708 --> 00:19:38,577
A freelance surgeon who has no insurance?

349
00:19:39,044 --> 00:19:41,713
That's insurance
if a surgery fails, right?

350
00:19:44,283 --> 00:19:46,585
I will not fail.

351
00:19:54,159 --> 00:19:56,161
Please take care.

352
00:20:07,072 --> 00:20:09,041
This is what Ms. Hanayama wants.

353
00:20:09,208 --> 00:20:11,176
I have to transfer her
to internal medicine.

354
00:20:13,111 --> 00:20:15,180
I never said anything.

355
00:20:16,415 --> 00:20:18,584
Why are you making excuses?

356
00:20:27,226 --> 00:20:29,127
Seems Dr. Daimon caused an uproar again.

357
00:20:29,628 --> 00:20:32,264
She's just a freelancer.
Why doesn't she quit?

358
00:20:32,331 --> 00:20:34,466
She also doesn't have
practicing doctor's insurance.

359
00:20:34,533 --> 00:20:36,668
- Really?
- I hope she goes bankrupt.

360
00:20:37,302 --> 00:20:39,404
As I remember,
Dr. Jonouchi had a rough time.

361
00:20:40,572 --> 00:20:43,842
That was clearly a false accusation.
You won the case, right?

362
00:20:43,909 --> 00:20:47,212
Even so, it went on for a year. I always
got called in and could hardly work.

363
00:20:47,279 --> 00:20:48,981
That was tough.

364
00:20:49,514 --> 00:20:51,250
Which was tougher? That or your divorce?

365
00:20:51,316 --> 00:20:53,685
Unlike your divorce, mine was amicable.

366
00:20:53,752 --> 00:20:54,586
Right.

367
00:20:57,990 --> 00:20:59,358
What's wrong, Morimoto?

368
00:21:00,926 --> 00:21:02,995
I've thought about it a lot lately,

369
00:21:03,595 --> 00:21:05,330
but if I was the patient,

370
00:21:05,831 --> 00:21:10,002
I would want a surgeon who's good
at surgery rather than a good talker,

371
00:21:10,936 --> 00:21:13,171
and if I was a patient being cut open,

372
00:21:13,405 --> 00:21:15,007
I'd want a surgeon with good hands,

373
00:21:15,073 --> 00:21:17,676
rather than a surgeon
with a good impression.

374
00:21:20,545 --> 00:21:22,748
Are you talking about Daimon?

375
00:21:24,549 --> 00:21:26,084
- N-no...
- When did you

376
00:21:26,151 --> 00:21:27,753
get brainwashed by Demon?

377
00:21:28,854 --> 00:21:30,622
That lady doctor is dangerous.

378
00:22:12,731 --> 00:22:16,001
I apologize for what happened
at the meeting.

379
00:22:17,135 --> 00:22:19,204
Was that supposed to be an apology?

380
00:22:20,372 --> 00:22:23,041
Thank goodness I switched
to internal medicine

381
00:22:23,108 --> 00:22:25,177
so I don't have to see you anymore.

382
00:22:25,243 --> 00:22:26,111
Ms. Hanayama.

383
00:22:28,113 --> 00:22:31,316
You should still have that surgery
as soon as possible.

384
00:22:34,953 --> 00:22:36,455
You're still saying that?

385
00:22:38,357 --> 00:22:40,625
For me, getting cured is to regain,

386
00:22:41,460 --> 00:22:44,429
to restore my delicate
and flawless sense of taste.

387
00:22:46,031 --> 00:22:47,466
Quality of life.

388
00:22:49,601 --> 00:22:50,969
It's natural for a pro.

389
00:22:51,036 --> 00:22:54,306
- Please listen to my pro surgeon adv--
- If you give more advice,

390
00:22:55,607 --> 00:22:57,042
I'll sue you for real.

391
00:23:13,558 --> 00:23:15,093
What's with you?

392
00:23:15,160 --> 00:23:18,830
Surely you're not trying
to up your girl power by learning to cook.

393
00:23:18,930 --> 00:23:19,798
No way.

394
00:23:21,199 --> 00:23:23,335
She goes to the dentist a lot.

395
00:23:26,571 --> 00:23:28,407
"I went to see a dentist again.

396
00:23:28,640 --> 00:23:32,377
I don't know if it was my imagination,
but my back right molar was hurting.

397
00:23:32,544 --> 00:23:34,980
But I didn't have cavities or gingivitis,

398
00:23:35,113 --> 00:23:37,783
and I was complimented
on my nice teeth."

399
00:23:37,849 --> 00:23:40,685
Her blog is all bragging, no?

400
00:23:40,752 --> 00:23:41,586
SEPTEMBER 4, 2011
WEDNESDAY

401
00:23:41,653 --> 00:23:42,988
But why are you reading this old entry?

402
00:23:43,455 --> 00:23:47,726
She should get surgery ASAP.
But she says she'll sue me.

403
00:23:47,793 --> 00:23:50,629
What? Are you getting sued?

404
00:23:51,496 --> 00:23:54,266
I just got a certified letter
from her lawyer.

405
00:23:57,235 --> 00:23:58,403
This is bad!

406
00:23:58,470 --> 00:24:01,840
How can you be reading a blog?
We have to do damage control!

407
00:24:13,351 --> 00:24:15,320
- I'll go get water.
- Yes.

408
00:24:22,527 --> 00:24:23,361
Hello?

409
00:24:23,428 --> 00:24:26,198
Ms. Hanayama, I apologize
for the phone call.

410
00:24:26,565 --> 00:24:29,301
I am Kambara,
Dr. Michiko Daimon's manager.

411
00:24:29,367 --> 00:24:33,071
<i>I apologize from the bottom of my heart</i>
<i>for any rudeness from us.</i>

412
00:24:33,138 --> 00:24:38,143
I was wondering if I could stop by
with a melon to apologize.

413
00:24:38,643 --> 00:24:42,747
With Daimon, of course. She would like
to offer her heartfelt apology as well.

414
00:24:42,814 --> 00:24:44,616
Why? I'm not doing it!

415
00:24:44,683 --> 00:24:46,084
I refuse.

416
00:24:46,818 --> 00:24:50,121
Just picturing that lady doctor's face
makes me nauseous.

417
00:24:50,589 --> 00:24:52,357
Please don't be like that.

418
00:24:53,191 --> 00:24:55,160
<i>I really feel like throwing up...</i>

419
00:24:55,894 --> 00:24:56,761
Hello?

420
00:24:57,195 --> 00:24:58,296
Uh, hello?

421
00:24:59,064 --> 00:25:01,066
What's wrong? She got quiet suddenly.

422
00:25:02,334 --> 00:25:03,168
Hello?

423
00:25:04,336 --> 00:25:05,170
Hello?

424
00:25:06,037 --> 00:25:06,872
<i>Ms. Hanayama?</i>

425
00:25:07,873 --> 00:25:08,874
<i>Ms. Hanayama?</i>

426
00:25:14,012 --> 00:25:15,680
Doctor! Doctor!

427
00:25:16,548 --> 00:25:17,482
Doctor!

428
00:25:17,549 --> 00:25:18,617
<i>Hello?</i>

429
00:25:18,817 --> 00:25:21,052
She said she was nauseous
and felt like throwing up.

430
00:25:26,758 --> 00:25:27,759
What about the melon?

431
00:25:44,309 --> 00:25:46,044
INTERNAL MEDICINE TREATMENT ROOM

432
00:25:46,111 --> 00:25:48,613
Arterial bleeding confirmed
at the esophageal cancer ward.

433
00:25:49,481 --> 00:25:50,749
What are you doing, Daimon?

434
00:25:51,016 --> 00:25:52,817
Hanayama coughed up blood, right?
Did you stop the bleeding?

435
00:25:52,884 --> 00:25:55,754
- We're trying with a clip, but...
- You're in the way. Move.

436
00:25:56,488 --> 00:25:58,823
This can't be stopped with an endoscope.
Take her to the OR immediately.

437
00:25:58,890 --> 00:26:00,492
- What?
- Emergency surgery.

438
00:26:02,294 --> 00:26:05,196
Wait! You're joking.
We don't have a consent form.

439
00:26:05,497 --> 00:26:06,498
Which OR is open?

440
00:26:06,865 --> 00:26:09,234
Wait, you can't!
Ms. Hanayama doesn't want surgery!

441
00:26:09,367 --> 00:26:11,870
Before surgery, we need consent
from the patient or their family!

442
00:26:13,138 --> 00:26:13,972
Huh?

443
00:26:14,639 --> 00:26:16,041
Dr. Daimon? It's your day off.

444
00:26:16,174 --> 00:26:17,976
We're starting surgery, call Dr. Jonouchi.

445
00:26:18,043 --> 00:26:20,178
- What surgery?
- Just call her now!

446
00:26:21,046 --> 00:26:21,913
Yes!

447
00:26:22,314 --> 00:26:23,148
No!

448
00:26:23,615 --> 00:26:27,485
- Get her family's consent first!
- While you say that, she'll die!

449
00:26:33,224 --> 00:26:34,559
<i>Anyways, please hurry!</i>

450
00:26:35,160 --> 00:26:36,828
Impossible. I can't today.

451
00:26:36,895 --> 00:26:39,197
Please!
It seems like an emergency surgery.

452
00:26:39,264 --> 00:26:41,366
Isn't there another anesthesiologist?

453
00:26:41,700 --> 00:26:43,335
<i>Other doctors are no good!</i>

454
00:26:43,401 --> 00:26:46,404
Dr. Daimon said to call Dr. Jonouchi ASAP.

455
00:26:46,471 --> 00:26:48,773
I told you I can't. I'm busy right now.

456
00:27:00,318 --> 00:27:02,654
Professor Torii. I apologize
for calling you on your day off.

457
00:27:03,121 --> 00:27:05,123
What? Surgery without consent?

458
00:27:05,690 --> 00:27:08,526
The patient is unconscious
and we can't contact her family.

459
00:27:09,227 --> 00:27:12,163
- She can't. Stop her.
- But if untreated, she may bleed to death.

460
00:27:12,230 --> 00:27:15,467
She can't do what she can't do.
Keep her alive with transfusion for now.

461
00:27:15,600 --> 00:27:17,769
If we do surgery without consent,
we'll be sued.

462
00:27:18,303 --> 00:27:19,137
Professor!

463
00:27:19,404 --> 00:27:20,538
AI OKUMURA
DR. TORII'S SECRETARY

464
00:27:20,605 --> 00:27:23,508
I made a reservation at a restaurant
and I want to go shopping, too.

465
00:27:24,976 --> 00:27:27,112
Do what you can to stop the surgery!

466
00:27:34,552 --> 00:27:36,287
ICU

467
00:27:41,760 --> 00:27:43,795
- Speed up the IV.
- Yes.

468
00:27:47,465 --> 00:27:50,035
- Suction inside the mouth.
- Understood.

469
00:27:55,840 --> 00:27:56,808
Please.

470
00:27:57,942 --> 00:27:58,910
Starting suction.

471
00:28:00,812 --> 00:28:02,447
Prepare for differential lung ventilation.

472
00:28:02,514 --> 00:28:04,416
DIFFERENTIAL LUNG VARIATION
A METHOD TO VENTILATE EACH LUNG SEPARATELY

473
00:28:04,649 --> 00:28:07,385
Won't we get in trouble for this?
We really don't have a consent form?

474
00:28:07,786 --> 00:28:09,788
What? You're kidding!

475
00:28:10,388 --> 00:28:12,724
This is non-compliance. I can't do it!

476
00:28:12,791 --> 00:28:15,627
- Position her on the left side.
- I refuse!

477
00:28:26,705 --> 00:28:27,706
Stop it!

478
00:28:32,477 --> 00:28:35,313
- What'll you do if you get sued?
- Dr. Jonouchi!

479
00:28:35,814 --> 00:28:38,216
- Prepare differential lung variation.
- Wait a minute.

480
00:28:39,017 --> 00:28:41,019
- You don't have insurance, right?
- Nope.

481
00:28:41,753 --> 00:28:43,154
MAP in units of 10. Hurry!

482
00:28:43,221 --> 00:28:44,756
Yes! Please.

483
00:28:45,223 --> 00:28:47,792
The hospital won't protect you, you know!

484
00:28:57,902 --> 00:28:58,737
No good!

485
00:29:00,271 --> 00:29:02,440
Hello? Hospital Chief!

486
00:29:02,841 --> 00:29:06,411
Yes, I heard from Professor Torii.

487
00:29:06,845 --> 00:29:11,449
Daimon is going to perform a surgery
without the patient's consent.

488
00:29:11,516 --> 00:29:14,319
I tried to stop her,
but it is true it's an emergency.

489
00:29:14,385 --> 00:29:17,055
- That's fine, no?
- What?

490
00:29:17,122 --> 00:29:20,558
Daimon isn't an official member
of our medical staff.

491
00:29:20,625 --> 00:29:22,193
If something happens,

492
00:29:22,360 --> 00:29:26,464
instead of the hospital, we'll have her
take responsibility herself.

493
00:29:27,031 --> 00:29:28,933
<i>If the surgery succeeds,</i>

494
00:29:29,267 --> 00:29:32,070
<i>our hospital's fame will rise again.</i>

495
00:29:33,972 --> 00:29:35,573
It's a good deal, no?

496
00:29:36,741 --> 00:29:38,743
Okay, I'm counting on you.

497
00:29:59,164 --> 00:30:00,965
- Anesthetics?
- Okay.

498
00:30:07,238 --> 00:30:08,473
- Wait.
- I can't wait.

499
00:30:09,207 --> 00:30:10,575
Let's at least contact her family.

500
00:30:10,642 --> 00:30:13,978
Which is more important,
the family's consent or her life?

501
00:30:26,958 --> 00:30:28,193
I'll be the first assistant.

502
00:30:29,127 --> 00:30:29,961
Yes.

503
00:30:30,829 --> 00:30:33,031
Arterial bleeding
due to esophageal cancer.

504
00:30:33,231 --> 00:30:36,067
We'll open the chest. After stopping
the bleeding, resect the esophagus.

505
00:30:36,668 --> 00:30:39,704
In addition, we'll open the stomach
and reconstruct using the colon.

506
00:30:39,771 --> 00:30:40,705
What?

507
00:30:42,273 --> 00:30:43,675
Reconstruct using the colon?

508
00:30:43,741 --> 00:30:44,809
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

509
00:30:52,784 --> 00:30:54,786
Forceps. Rib shear.

510
00:31:00,859 --> 00:31:02,861
First assistant.
Hurry and get the forceps.

511
00:31:04,095 --> 00:31:05,396
Give me the forceps.

512
00:31:12,303 --> 00:31:14,038
Hurry up and expose the ribs.

513
00:31:17,508 --> 00:31:18,409
Rib spreader.

514
00:32:02,086 --> 00:32:03,121
Hello?

515
00:32:03,187 --> 00:32:04,055
Mai?

516
00:32:04,489 --> 00:32:06,724
Sorry Mama had to leave in the middle.

517
00:32:07,492 --> 00:32:08,726
Did you fall while running?

518
00:32:08,793 --> 00:32:12,163
I didn't fall, Mama. First place!

519
00:32:12,230 --> 00:32:15,867
First place? That's awesome, you did it!

520
00:32:16,401 --> 00:32:20,505
I'll be there as soon as I can,
so listen to your teacher and be good.

521
00:32:20,905 --> 00:32:22,974
Yeah. Okay!

522
00:32:31,950 --> 00:32:33,084
Your daughter?

523
00:32:34,953 --> 00:32:38,122
You call me on weekends again,
I'll hang up on you. 

524
00:32:41,526 --> 00:32:43,061
Thanks for your hard work.

525
00:32:57,008 --> 00:32:58,910
#2 SURGERY PROFESSOR'S OFFICE
TAKASHI TORII

526
00:33:12,590 --> 00:33:13,458
Excuse me.

527
00:33:15,193 --> 00:33:16,060
Hara.

528
00:33:16,761 --> 00:33:18,363
This is Ms. Hanayama's lawyer.

529
00:33:19,764 --> 00:33:24,235
I'd like to hear in detail about
the surgery done without consent.

530
00:33:27,238 --> 00:33:30,308
She almost died from hemorrhagic shock.

531
00:33:31,175 --> 00:33:33,911
The surgery was necessary
to stop the bleeding.

532
00:33:33,978 --> 00:33:35,146
How is she now?

533
00:33:35,313 --> 00:33:38,649
She was in critical condition for a while,
but she's stable now.

534
00:33:40,218 --> 00:33:43,154
Thank you for saving her life.

535
00:33:45,156 --> 00:33:50,528
However, Ms. Hanayama refused the surgery
to preserve her other life, her work.

536
00:33:51,696 --> 00:33:54,699
Once she regains consciousness,
we will file a lawsuit.

537
00:33:54,766 --> 00:33:55,867
What?

538
00:33:58,503 --> 00:34:02,206
You knew you could be sued
even if you saved a life!

539
00:34:04,475 --> 00:34:05,343
Say something!

540
00:34:08,546 --> 00:34:09,414
You can't sue us.

541
00:34:10,681 --> 00:34:11,549
What?

542
00:34:11,949 --> 00:34:16,154
Dr. Daimon didn't perform
the surgery Ms. Hanayama refused.

543
00:34:17,588 --> 00:34:18,823
What do you mean?

544
00:34:20,491 --> 00:34:23,861
The surgery I had originally planned

545
00:34:24,695 --> 00:34:28,433
was esophagectomy with gastric tube
reconstruction by stretching the stomach.

546
00:34:29,067 --> 00:34:30,401
ESOPHAGUS - STOMACH
GASTRIC TUBE RECONSTRUCTION

547
00:34:30,468 --> 00:34:33,104
In that case,
there's a risk of post-surgery disorders,

548
00:34:33,204 --> 00:34:36,874
such as trouble swallowing,
which would have affected her work.

549
00:34:38,843 --> 00:34:41,879
<i>However, the method used</i>
<i>by Dr. Daimon today</i>

550
00:34:42,346 --> 00:34:46,684
<i>used the colon and not the stomach</i>
<i>to reconstruct the esophagus.</i>

551
00:34:47,318 --> 00:34:49,687
<i>Gastric function keeping</i>
<i>esophageal reconstruction.</i>

552
00:34:50,288 --> 00:34:51,856
It's a very difficult operation...

553
00:34:51,923 --> 00:34:53,391
ESOPHAGUS, STOMACH, COLON - GASTRIC
FUNCTION KEEPING ESOPHAGEAL RECONSTRUCTION

554
00:34:53,458 --> 00:34:57,361
...but since it keeps the stomach
to preserve gastric functions,

555
00:34:57,762 --> 00:34:59,597
<i>it seems to be the best method.</i>

556
00:35:00,731 --> 00:35:04,669
<i>Ms. Hanayama's esophageal cancer</i>
<i>has been completely removed.</i>

557
00:35:12,376 --> 00:35:13,678
Her condition is stable.

558
00:35:15,113 --> 00:35:19,250
I believe she can continue
her normal activities as a cooking expert.

559
00:35:21,819 --> 00:35:23,821
Are you still going to file a lawsuit?

560
00:35:34,265 --> 00:35:37,735
I'll talk with her about it
once she wakes up.

561
00:35:40,738 --> 00:35:42,573
Thank you very much!

562
00:35:42,807 --> 00:35:44,542
Thank you very much!

563
00:35:49,447 --> 00:35:52,650
Did she really perform
such a flawless surgery?

564
00:35:55,286 --> 00:35:56,287
Yes.

565
00:36:09,800 --> 00:36:13,271
Ah, this feels good!

566
00:36:19,844 --> 00:36:22,547
ONE WEEK LATER

567
00:36:22,613 --> 00:36:27,985
<i>From now, Professor Busujima will make</i>
<i>the Chief's rounds of the surgery ward.</i>

568
00:36:30,521 --> 00:36:34,258
Daimon's surgery seemed to go well, right?

569
00:36:34,325 --> 00:36:36,494
Yes, recovery is going well, too.

570
00:36:36,561 --> 00:36:38,462
That's excellent.

571
00:36:43,968 --> 00:36:45,570
Chief!

572
00:36:46,237 --> 00:36:47,171
Excuse me.

573
00:36:47,538 --> 00:36:49,840
- What's wrong?
- It was all for nothing.

574
00:36:49,907 --> 00:36:52,410
The lawyer says they're suing.

575
00:36:52,476 --> 00:36:54,478
Wasn't Daimon's surgery successful?

576
00:36:54,545 --> 00:36:55,646
It was.

577
00:36:55,713 --> 00:36:59,150
But it must mean the patient
wasn't satisfied with the result.

578
00:36:59,617 --> 00:37:01,986
- Well, it can't be helped.
- What?

579
00:37:03,854 --> 00:37:06,457
The hospital claims no responsibility.

580
00:37:07,325 --> 00:37:11,162
Daimon, who performed the surgery
on her own, will be held accountable.

581
00:37:11,229 --> 00:37:12,530
Ah, certainly.

582
00:37:21,639 --> 00:37:24,308
Michiko, this is bad.
We're really in trouble.

583
00:37:24,375 --> 00:37:29,647
"Dr. Michiko Daimon of Teito Medical
University Third Hospital #2 Surgery

584
00:37:30,147 --> 00:37:32,149
with regards to Mitsue Hanayama,

585
00:37:32,216 --> 00:37:36,520
performed surgery to remove esophageal
cancer without consent with explanation.

586
00:37:36,587 --> 00:37:39,724
As a result of the surgery,

587
00:37:40,091 --> 00:37:42,493
the patient is suffering
from a taste disorder

588
00:37:42,560 --> 00:37:46,464
and other post-surgery effects.

589
00:37:47,198 --> 00:37:48,266
Due to this,

590
00:37:48,966 --> 00:37:54,405
it has become difficult for the patient
to continue activities as a cooking expert

591
00:37:54,772 --> 00:38:00,578
and she is in danger
of losing her career and her fame.

592
00:38:01,379 --> 00:38:04,548
<i>The patient hereby demands</i>
<i>that Dr. Daimon,</i>

593
00:38:05,249 --> 00:38:08,452
along with the Teito Medical University
Third Hospital,

594
00:38:08,919 --> 00:38:10,855
make a payment

595
00:38:11,322 --> 00:38:13,391
in the amount of 100 million yen

596
00:38:13,457 --> 00:38:16,994
to the patient to compensate for damages."

597
00:38:20,965 --> 00:38:22,566
Taste disorder...

598
00:38:23,134 --> 00:38:24,535
100 million yen...

599
00:38:29,807 --> 00:38:33,344
What the hell is this?
It has no taste! I can't eat this!

600
00:38:33,411 --> 00:38:36,280
It's porridge,
it only has light seasoning.

601
00:38:37,181 --> 00:38:38,949
I said I don't want to eat it!

602
00:38:51,629 --> 00:38:52,463
It's very good.

603
00:38:53,397 --> 00:38:55,499
Because of the surgery,
I can't taste anything!

604
00:38:55,833 --> 00:38:57,968
My life is ruined because of you!

605
00:38:58,903 --> 00:38:59,804
Ms. Hanayama.

606
00:39:00,871 --> 00:39:03,307
That started before the surgery, no?

607
00:39:06,711 --> 00:39:11,882
You noticed symptoms of a taste disorder
about a year ago, right?

608
00:39:14,685 --> 00:39:19,256
But as a cooking pro, you had to fake it
so people around you wouldn't notice.

609
00:39:20,624 --> 00:39:22,526
Dr. Daimon, what are you saying?

610
00:39:28,332 --> 00:39:31,469
Your blog... I read all of it.

611
00:39:32,169 --> 00:39:37,441
You saw the dentist a few times last year
complaining of a toothache, right?

612
00:39:40,077 --> 00:39:42,012
But the pain isn't from a tooth.

613
00:39:43,347 --> 00:39:45,549
It's not related
to the esophageal cancer either.

614
00:39:46,083 --> 00:39:48,386
Then what is it?

615
00:39:50,888 --> 00:39:53,124
It's glossopharyngeal neuralgia.

616
00:39:54,692 --> 00:39:55,526
What is that?

617
00:39:57,661 --> 00:40:00,364
A tumor forms on
the membrane encasing cerebral nerves...

618
00:40:00,431 --> 00:40:01,832
CEREBRAL NERVES
GLOSSOPHARYNGEAL NEURALGIA

619
00:40:01,899 --> 00:40:04,668
...putting pressure on them
and causing a taste disorder.

620
00:40:06,971 --> 00:40:11,442
None of the doctors here
mentioned anything about a tumor.

621
00:40:12,743 --> 00:40:16,147
They were focused on the cancer
and overlooked it.

622
00:40:17,381 --> 00:40:20,684
It bothered me a little
so I asked to see an image.

623
00:40:23,087 --> 00:40:24,422
- Who is that?
- Huh?

624
00:40:24,655 --> 00:40:26,424
I'm Shiraki from Radiology.

625
00:40:26,857 --> 00:40:28,459
I'm Shiraki from Radiology.

626
00:40:33,531 --> 00:40:36,467
It's hard to tell,
but can you see this spot here?

627
00:40:43,340 --> 00:40:45,242
Is this... also cancer?

628
00:40:45,543 --> 00:40:48,879
Ninety-eight percent of the tumor
in glossopharyngeal neuralgia is benign.

629
00:40:48,946 --> 00:40:50,714
If it's still this size after a year...

630
00:40:50,781 --> 00:40:52,383
I'm sure it's benign.

631
00:40:59,523 --> 00:41:00,357
I see.

632
00:41:02,293 --> 00:41:05,496
But... how did you find it

633
00:41:06,530 --> 00:41:08,499
when other doctors overlooked it?

634
00:41:10,801 --> 00:41:13,003
Because the food you cooked
tasted so bad.

635
00:41:14,171 --> 00:41:15,840
You're really a rude doctor.

636
00:41:15,906 --> 00:41:20,077
But the food you made
more than a year ago was exquisite.

637
00:41:21,679 --> 00:41:22,613
Well, thanks.

638
00:41:25,316 --> 00:41:30,387
If you have surgery to remove the tumor,
the taste disorder will be cured.

639
00:41:37,528 --> 00:41:41,131
My sense of taste from then...
will return?

640
00:41:45,703 --> 00:41:46,570
Really?

641
00:41:48,606 --> 00:41:49,907
Let me do the surgery.

642
00:41:54,445 --> 00:41:57,014
I will not fail.

643
00:42:05,823 --> 00:42:10,060
Well, since the scar
from your surgery is clean,

644
00:42:12,162 --> 00:42:13,531
maybe I will.

645
00:42:20,838 --> 00:42:22,206
I'm counting on you.

646
00:42:45,095 --> 00:42:47,064
DOCTOR REFERRAL
KAMBARA

647
00:42:47,131 --> 00:42:48,933
BEN CASEY

648
00:42:52,636 --> 00:42:53,470
Hey, Michiko.

649
00:42:54,104 --> 00:42:56,540
You got a new cooking book
from Ms. Hanayama.

650
00:42:57,007 --> 00:42:59,677
- I don't care.
- I'll read her letter out loud.

651
00:43:00,110 --> 00:43:01,912
"Dr. Daimon, how are you?

652
00:43:02,146 --> 00:43:05,883
I, Mitsue Hanayama,
recently became married with Dr. Nakano

653
00:43:05,950 --> 00:43:09,787
in internal medicine after courtship.
I met him during my hospital stay."

654
00:43:10,220 --> 00:43:11,989
- What?
- Here, a picture.

655
00:43:12,923 --> 00:43:15,159
"My cooking knocked him down.

656
00:43:15,559 --> 00:43:18,629
I wanted to share my happiness
with Dr. Daimon,

657
00:43:18,862 --> 00:43:21,065
so please try cooking every now and then.

658
00:43:21,131 --> 00:43:25,135
My recommendation for you is on page 36.

659
00:43:31,675 --> 00:43:33,744
Girl power apple pie."

660
00:43:36,647 --> 00:43:37,648
Don't mess with me.

661
00:43:41,986 --> 00:43:43,520
You have zero girl power.

662
00:43:48,592 --> 00:43:50,794
<i>She hates groups, she hates authority,</i>

663
00:43:50,961 --> 00:43:52,496
<i>and she hates constraints.</i>

664
00:43:52,963 --> 00:43:57,101
<i>Her weapons are her specialty license</i>
<i>and her skill to work her way up.</i>

665
00:43:58,369 --> 00:44:01,271
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

666
00:44:03,407 --> 00:44:04,341
<i>Also known as...</i>

667
00:44:10,014 --> 00:44:12,182
Ms. Hanayama sent us
some food to thank us.

668
00:44:13,617 --> 00:44:16,954
"To all the single doctors:
Carnivore Male Power UPple Meat Pie."

669
00:44:17,454 --> 00:44:18,322
Huh?

670
00:44:18,522 --> 00:44:22,559
Carnivore Male Power Up with UPple?
Ms. Hanayama...

671
00:44:24,728 --> 00:44:25,629
Tasty!

672
00:44:26,563 --> 00:44:28,699
Yeah, it's so good.

673
00:44:29,199 --> 00:44:31,435
She even cured her taste disorder.

674
00:44:35,139 --> 00:44:37,074
You still talking about Demon?

675
00:44:37,808 --> 00:44:42,046
There's no way she can do
one flawless surgery after another.

676
00:44:43,447 --> 00:44:44,314
Delicious!

677
00:44:45,249 --> 00:44:46,850
Well, it's okay.

678
00:44:47,985 --> 00:44:49,353
Dr. Kaji!

679
00:44:49,420 --> 00:44:51,989
You remember the story
of that mysterious doctor?

680
00:44:52,056 --> 00:44:54,224
Yeah. That amazing surgeon in Cuba?

681
00:44:54,291 --> 00:44:55,626
There's more to the story.

682
00:45:01,699 --> 00:45:05,269
The patient who had this surgery
died one month later.

683
00:45:05,669 --> 00:45:10,107
<i>Surviving family members filed a lawsuit</i>
<i>against the hospital to find the cause.</i>

684
00:45:10,507 --> 00:45:13,644
However, to this day, the hospital

685
00:45:13,711 --> 00:45:18,015
has not released the identity
of the primary surgeon, Doctor X.

686
00:45:30,694 --> 00:45:32,830
Subtitle translation by Paul Koehler

687
00:45:33,397 --> 00:45:35,199
I call it a laparoscopic/endoscopic
hybrid surgery.

688
00:45:35,265 --> 00:45:36,100
NEXT EPISODE

689
00:45:36,200 --> 00:45:37,701
THE TIME LIMIT IS 49 HOURS

690
00:45:37,768 --> 00:45:39,103
I've never seen or heard
of such a reckless surgery.

691
00:45:39,169 --> 00:45:40,704
- Can you really do that?
- How many arms do you have?

692
00:45:40,771 --> 00:45:41,672
IS ALL OF THIS A TRAP!?

693
00:45:41,739 --> 00:45:43,741
- There's no way you can do it.
- I can do it.

694
00:45:43,807 --> 00:45:44,708
Daimon!

695
00:45:44,775 --> 00:45:45,909
I can't do it. This is impossible!

696
00:45:45,976 --> 00:45:46,844
This drama is fiction. All names of people
and organizations are fictional.

697
00:45:46,910 --> 00:45:47,745
Medical practices in the drama vary
depending on a person's medical condition.
